35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The prefecture beds are only 1,100 yen a night! That’s incredibly cheap. But the inland clubs slept eight to a room.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The seniors say mixing only happens in shared evenings. And a third of us need a bed before nine. We must stay together.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The canteen closure means two hours daily cooking duty. A place with kitchen staff eliminates that. I need to avoid that burden.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,Our own hall is booked by three other clubs. Training would be split into early mornings and late evenings. That is not a real camp.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The transport receipts show the bus was thirty-eight percent of the total cost. The inland clubs had strict curfews. I need to see if we can avoid that rigidity.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, thirty-eight percent is huge! If we pick the cheap prefecture beds, we save money, but do we still have to pay for the bus separately?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, the seniors say mixing only happens in shared evenings. If we stay together, we build those bonds.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the lottery is a trap. A nine-page application resubmitted if one date shifts. I cannot risk that administrative burden.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree. The whole-building quote is fixed weeks ahead with a non-refundable deposit. If someone drops out, we all pay for their empty bed.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, yes. The bus cost is fixed regardless of the destination. I need to ensure the per-head bed fee covers the actual room costs, not just the transport.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Rin, that non-refundable deposit is exactly my fear! If someone cancels, who eats that loss? I need a clear rule before we book.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, I understand the worry. But if we stay together, the seniors say the year-groups finally talk. I hope we can find a fair way to share that risk.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, shared evenings are good, but I need to know if the duty schedule allows for actual rest. I cannot repeat last year’s exhaustion.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree. Rest is non-negotiable. If the hall is split, I’m out. I need a place where we can actually sleep properly.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I agree. Rest is essential. I will ensure the budget covers the actual costs so we do not carry this deficit forward.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’m leaning toward the prefecture beds. They are cheap and simple. But we must agree on a cancellation rule before booking.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am leaning toward the prefecture beds too. The seniors say shared evenings are where we truly connect. Let us hope the cost allows for that warmth.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am leaning toward a place with kitchen staff. The lottery is too risky, and I refuse to cook for two hours daily.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I am leaning toward a whole-building let. It guarantees private, quiet rooms for everyone. No shared noise, no split schedules. Just proper sleep.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I am leaning toward the prefecture beds. The low per-head cost is the only way to close the account gap without raising fees.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
